<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49006" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭbūtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		tribuo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A dividing</i>, <i>distributing</i>,
				<i>distribution</i> (very rare): hanc <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσονομίαν</span> appellat Epicurus, id est
			aequabilem tributionem, * <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				1, 19, 50</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tributio fit pro ratā ejus, quod
					cuique debetur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					14, 4, 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A contributing</i>, <i>paying of
				tribute</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 2, 14, 52</span></i>; <i><span class="en">50, 4, 18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
